From: MGS2 RG353VS compatibility port
Subject: [PATCH] libdg: isolate the fixed-function wpatch fallback

FINALPLAY21 disabled the custom wpatch vertex shader globally because the
DXVK/Mali route did not render the animated sea.  The recovered call census
shows one other external wpatch consumer: the no-wrap IPU movie panel.  Keep
that panel on the original vertex-shader path while retaining the existing
fixed-function fallback for the water consumers.

The fixed-function branch enables D3D8 lighting and installs patch-local light
state.  Return lighting to libdg's disabled baseline at the plugin tail so a
later fixed-function draw cannot inherit the last water light.

The distributed 2003 executable is not stored in this repository.  The
fail-closed runtime equivalent validates the original instructions and an
unused executable tail, applies only the recorded branch/trampoline bytes to a
temporary image, expands .text's virtual extent within its existing raw size,
and verifies the complete output hash.

--- a/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/wdgd.c
+++ b/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/wdgd.c
@@ -1459,7 +1459,6 @@
 			}
 			DG_WinApp.flag |= M_DG_WINAPP_SHADOWWT_USE_VERTEXSHADER ;
 			DG_WinApp.flag |= M_DG_WINAPP_OPTCMF00_USE_VERTEXSHADER ;
-			DG_WinApp.flag |= M_DG_WINAPP_PATCH_USE_VERTEXSHADER ;
 
 			/* DG_EVMOBJ描画VertexShader使用判定  */
 			if(  X2W_GetAppConfig(X2WAPPCFG_EVM_USE_OBJ_MULTITEX) )
--- a/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/wpatch.c
+++ b/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/wpatch.c
@@ -1124,7 +1124,8 @@
 		DG_SetAlphaMode(0);
 	}
 
-	if( DG_CheckPatchUseVertexShader() )
+	if( DG_CheckPatchUseVertexShader()
+	 || ( patch->flag & DG_PATCH_NO_WRAP ) )
 	{
 		{/* 環境マッピング用マトリクスの設定 */
 			FMATRIX		mat ;
@@ -1608,6 +1609,7 @@
 
 	DG_SetTextureStageState(0, D3DTSS_ADDRESSU, D3DTADDRESS_CLAMP);
 	DG_SetTextureStageState(0, D3DTSS_ADDRESSV, D3DTADDRESS_CLAMP);
+	DG_SetRenderState(D3DRS_LIGHTING, FALSE);
 
 	/* スタティックプッシュバッファへの記録終了 */
 	DG_CloseDmaTask();
